1. `dims` is `DimensionIndex[]` (= `number[]`), so `'x'` and `['x', 'y']` are type errors, and the
   "no dims" overload `each(function (idx) {})` does not exist here — the array form `each([], cb)`
   is what produces the index-only callback (see the `case 0:` branch below).
2. There is no `ctx` parameter at all, yet `@param ctx default this` is present. Contrast with
   `SeriesData#each`, which really does take `ctx`.
3. The receiver is named `list`, but this class is `DataStore`, not `SeriesData`/`List`.

The implementation confirming (1), `/workspace/src/data/DataStore.ts:1095-1128`:

```ts
    each(dims: DimensionIndex[], cb: EachCb): void {
        if (!this._count) {
            return;
        }
        const dimSize = dims.length;
        const chunks = this._chunks;

        for (let i = 0, len = this.count(); i < len; i++) {
            const rawIdx = this.getRawIndex(i);
            // Simple optimization
            switch (dimSize) {
                case 0:
                    (cb as EachCb0)(i);
                    break;
                case 1:
                    (cb as EachCb1)(chunks[dims[0]][rawIdx], i);
                    break;
                case 2:
                    (cb as EachCb2)(
                        chunks[dims[0]][rawIdx], chunks[dims[1]][rawIdx], i
                    );
                    break;
                default:
                    let k = 0;
                    const value = [];
                    for (; k < dimSize; k++) {
                        value[k] = chunks[dims[k]][rawIdx];
                    }
                    // Index
                    value[k] = i;
                    (cb as EachCb).apply(null, value);
            }
        }
    }
```

`dims[0]` is used directly as a key into `this._chunks` (a `DataValueChunk[]` indexed by store
dimension index), so only numbers are meaningful.

`DataStore` callback types, `/workspace/src/data/DataStore.ts:64-67`:

```ts
type EachCb0 = (idx: number) => void;
type EachCb1 = (x: ParsedValue, idx: number) => void;
type EachCb2 = (x: ParsedValue, y: ParsedValue, idx: number) => void;
type EachCb = (...args: any) => void;
```

### 2.3 Scope check — these are the only two occurrences

```
$ grep -rn "list.each(" /workspace/src /workspace/test --include=*.ts --include=*.js --include=*.html
/workspace/src/data/SeriesData.ts:885
/workspace/src/data/SeriesData.ts:886
